@packages/cli import { SigilCli }

component SigilCompilationExecution {
  goal {
    Execute ordinary Sigil compilation reproducibly and retain one compiler-owned
    Markdown report without consuming a live event stream or deciding the design or
    implementation question being evaluated.
  }

  interface {
CompilationExecution {
      runs one selected SigilCli target with the effective agent profile and either
      design or implementation compilation focus

      reserves a fresh Markdown output path outside the workspace for each attempt
      and preserves its exit status and stderr evidence through review completion

      returns a readable completed Markdown report, failure, cancellation, or host
      failure to the calling workflow for focus-specific interpretation
    }
  }
}

expand SigilCompilationExecution {
  logic {
CompilationExecution {
      Reserve a task-scoped temporary directory and a unique nonexistent report path
      for each attempt. Run SigilCli with `--agent --focus <design|implementation>
      --format markdown --output <report-path>` and wait for the launched process to
      exit.

      Accept a completed compilation only when the process exits with the completed
      report exit class and the attempt's fresh output is readable and nonempty. Read
      that file as the compiler-owned Markdown projection and return it with the exit
      status. Do not listen to, parse, capture, or recover a JSONL event stream.

      After process exit, retry the identical target once when a runtime failure,
      abnormal termination, missing output, unreadable output, or empty output
      prevents completed-report evidence.
    }
  }

  constraints {
CompilationExecution {
      `--agent` selects the effective agent profile and never combines with
      `--profile`. Compiler sessions are reserved for explicitly requested
      exceptional diagnostics.

      Stdout, progress, silence, slow execution, passing tests, and the mere presence
      of an output path do not establish compilation evidence.

      Exit zero or one with the attempt's readable nonempty report is a completed
      green, yellow, or red report and is returned for focus-specific interpretation;
      exit one is not automatically a failure because completed yellow and red
      reports use it. Exit two is an invocation defect that must be corrected rather
      than retried identically. Exit 130 is cancellation and is not retried
      automatically. Exit three, another abnormal termination, or an invalid report
      artifact is an incomplete operational outcome and receives one identical retry.
      The second failed or incomplete attempt blocks its calling workflow.

      A report path must not exist before its attempt. A report artifact is never
      accepted when its process exits outside the completed report exit class, even
      if a file exists, so stale or partially settled output cannot become evidence.

      An identical retry preserves the source snapshot identity, focus, target
      selector, resolved effective profile, and material invocation options. If those
      inputs cannot be frozen, report a host failure instead of claiming
      reproducibility.

      Host failure is the single returned host failure identity for an unreadable or
      invalid report artifact, inability to freeze retry inputs, or inability to
      reserve an isolated output destination.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    SharedCompilationExecution {
      Decision: Centralize ordinary compile execution around process completion and a
      fresh compiler-owned Markdown output while callers retain target selection and
      focus-specific report interpretation.

      Scope: Governs design and implementation compilation in the Sigil skill;
      excludes compiler evaluation semantics and review or implementation approval.

      Trade-offs: Callers add one dependency and lose live event progress, but no
      longer duplicate stream listeners, event recovery, or retry behavior.

      Design issues addressed: Parallel compile instructions drifted despite sharing
      the same invocation and terminal-evidence requirements.

      Discarded alternatives: JSONL stream consumption and stdout-only Markdown
      capture were rejected because ordinary review needs one durable completed
      artifact rather than event recovery or transient presentation output.

      Consequences: Both workflows use the agent profile and a fresh Markdown output
      artifact, differing only in compilation focus and interpretation. Failed or
      incomplete operational runs receive one identical retry after process exit.
    }
  }
}
